{"diagnosis": "Loopback send 0xa5 was sampled as 0xff idle, causing TRAP uart data mismatch and tohost FAIL 0xdead. ser_tx is corrupted by the send_dummy branch loading send_pattern <= ~1 whose LSB 0 injects a false start bit with send_bitcnt <= 15 shortening idle. The receiver stays busy/misaligned on the dummy frame when the real {1'b1, reg_dat_di[7:0], 1'b0} frame starts, so recv_pattern samples idle 1s.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -118,7 +118,7 @@
 		end else begin
 			if (send_dummy && !send_bitcnt) begin
-				send_pattern <= ~1;
-				send_bitcnt <= 15;
+				send_pattern <= ~0;
+				send_bitcnt <= 16;
 				send_divcnt <= 0;
 				send_dummy <= 0;
 			end else
", "expected": "tohost PASS - tb_picosoc_uart divider 64 loopback 0xa5 received correctly, no TRAP uart data mismatch"}

